{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"121156","commit":"7ec35340c310ebde975531d609e35f61c4807bdf","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `RemoveRedundantSort` rule assumes that any `OrderBy` before a `TopN` is redundant if it\u0027s not followed by operations that could make the sort relevant again (like window functions). However, this assumption might be too broad. For example, sorting by different fields in consecutive `OrderBy` clauses can lead to different results even if the second sort is bounded by a `TopN`. This rule should be more cautious and consider cases where multiple sorts are necessary for correctness.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalVerifier.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalVerifier.java--1087:1228","promptId":"#177WF","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalVerifier.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalVerifier.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1087,"endPos":1228,"startLine":30,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":32,"endLineOffset":17,"length":142}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java--326999:328421,328427:329265,329271:330428,330434:331630,331636:333295,333301:335312,335318:335967","promptId":"#9ACG3","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":326999,"endPos":328421,"startLine":7272,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7301,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1423},{"pos":328427,"endPos":329265,"startLine":7303,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7325,"endLineOffset":5,"length":839},{"pos":329271,"endPos":330428,"startLine":7327,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7353,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1158},{"pos":330434,"endPos":331630,"startLine":7355,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7382,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1197},{"pos":331636,"endPos":333295,"startLine":7384,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7417,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1660},{"pos":333301,"endPos":335312,"startLine":7419,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7456,"endLineOffset":5,"length":2012},{"pos":335318,"endPos":335967,"startLine":7458,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7473,"endLineOffset":5,"length":650}]},{"id":"-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/rules/logical/RemoveRedundantSort.java--0:252,1014:3357","promptId":"#ZHWJ6","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/rules/logical/RemoveRedundantSort.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":0,"endPos":252,"startLine":1,"startLineOffset":0,"endLine":6,"endLineOffset":3,"length":253},{"pos":1014,"endPos":3357,"startLine":23,"startLineOffset":0,"endLine":88,"endLineOffset":1,"length":2344}]}]},{"comment":"The `postOptimizationVerification` method in `OrderBy` always adds a failure indicating an unbounded sort without checking if the sort is actually unbounded after optimizations. This could lead to false positives where the sort might have been transformed into a bounded one by other rules.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/OrderBy.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/OrderBy.java--3606:3793","promptId":"#R1ZB8","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/OrderBy.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/OrderBy.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3606,"endPos":3793,"startLine":114,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":117,"endLineOffset":5,"length":188}]}]},{"comment":"The test cases added (`testRedundantSortOnJoin`, `testRedundantSortOnMvExpand`, etc.) are good for verifying that redundant sorts are removed, but they do not cover scenarios where multiple sorts are necessary or where the sort is not actually redundant. Additional test cases should be added to ensure these edge cases are handled correctly.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java--326999:328421,328427:329265,329271:330428,330434:331630,331636:333295,333301:335312,335318:335967","promptId":"#9ACG3","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":326999,"endPos":328421,"startLine":7272,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7301,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1423},{"pos":328427,"endPos":329265,"startLine":7303,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7325,"endLineOffset":5,"length":839},{"pos":329271,"endPos":330428,"startLine":7327,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7353,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1158},{"pos":330434,"endPos":331630,"startLine":7355,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7382,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1197},{"pos":331636,"endPos":333295,"startLine":7384,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7417,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1660},{"pos":333301,"endPos":335312,"startLine":7419,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7456,"endLineOffset":5,"length":2012},{"pos":335318,"endPos":335967,"startLine":7458,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7473,"endLineOffset":5,"length":650}]}]},{"comment":"The `testUnboundedSort` case checks for an unbounded sort scenario, which is good. However, it would be beneficial to have more detailed assertions on the exception message or stack trace to ensure that the correct part of the query is identified as causing the issue.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java--326999:328421,328427:329265,329271:330428,330434:331630,331636:333295,333301:335312,335318:335967","promptId":"#9ACG3","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":326999,"endPos":328421,"startLine":7272,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7301,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1423},{"pos":328427,"endPos":329265,"startLine":7303,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7325,"endLineOffset":5,"length":839},{"pos":329271,"endPos":330428,"startLine":7327,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7353,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1158},{"pos":330434,"endPos":331630,"startLine":7355,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7382,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1197},{"pos":331636,"endPos":333295,"startLine":7384,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7417,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1660},{"pos":333301,"endPos":335312,"startLine":7419,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7456,"endLineOffset":5,"length":2012},{"pos":335318,"endPos":335967,"startLine":7458,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":7473,"endLineOffset":5,"length":650}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":1844,"line":1844,"comment_lines":["[1844][]"],"review_comment":["Notice that here you are losing a performance aspect: `mv_expand` is applied on all documents. The idea with a sort (and the **default** pushed down `limit`) in front of `mv_expand` was to have fewer documents to expand from because the expansion is, theoretically, creating even more rows. Before this PR, each node was getting 1000 docs, mv_expanded them and a final sort performed. With this PR, each node is expanding everything, then sorting.","Yes, but you were also discarding all the employees after the first 1000 (sorted by emp_no), that is not what the query says, so technically you got a faster execution, but a wrong result."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","id":36731,"created_at":"2025-01-30T13:48:44Z","original_position":6,"side":"LEFT","position":14,"submitted_on_commit":"7ec35340c310ebde975531d609e35f61c4807bdf","diff_hunk":"@@ -1839,10 +1839,9 @@ public void testCombineOrderByThroughFilter() {\n \n     /**\n      * Expected\n-     * TopN[[Order[first_name{f}#170,ASC,LAST]],1000[INTEGER]]\n-     *  \\_MvExpand[first_name{f}#170]\n-     *    \\_TopN[[Order[emp_no{f}#169,ASC,LAST]],1000[INTEGER]]","submitted_line":1844},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]}],"coveredGroundTruth":0,"uncoveredGroundTruth":1,"coveredMatchable":4,"uncoveredMatchable":12,"timing":76995,"tokensIn":13644,"tokensOut":723}